#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A window function that returns a cluster number for each input geometry, "
"using the 2D <link "
"xlink:href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DBSCAN\">Density-based spatial "
"clustering of applications with noise (DBSCAN)</link> algorithm. Unlike "
"<xref linkend=\"ST_ClusterKMeans\"/>, it does not require the number of "
"clusters to be specified, but instead uses the desired <link "
"linkend=\"ST_Distance\">distance</link> (<varname>eps</varname>) and density"
" (<varname>minpoints</varname>) parameters to determine each cluster."
msgstr ""
"En fönsterfunktion som returnerar ett klusternummer för varje indatageometri"
" med 2D-algoritmen <link "
"xlink:href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DBSCAN\">Density-based spatial "
"clustering of applications with noise (DBSCAN)</link>. Till skillnad från "
"<xref linkend=\"ST_ClusterKMeans\"/> kräver den inte att antalet kluster "
"anges, utan använder i stället parametrarna för önskat <link "
"linkend=\"ST_Distance\">distance</link> (<varname>eps</varname>) och "
"densitet (<varname>minpoints</varname>) för att bestämma varje kluster."

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"ST_ClusterWithin is equivalent to running <xref "
"linkend=\"ST_ClusterDBSCAN\"/> with <code>minpoints =&gt; 0</code>."
msgstr ""
"ST_ClusterWithin motsvarar att köra <xref linkend=\"ST_ClusterDBSCAN\"/> med"
" <code>minpoints =&gt; 0</code>."

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A window function that returns a cluster number for each input geometry. "
"Clustering partitions the geometries into sets in which each geometry is "
"within the specified <varname>distance</varname> of at least one other "
"geometry in the same cluster. Distances are Cartesian distances in the units"
" of the SRID."
msgstr ""
"En fönsterfunktion som returnerar ett klusternummer för varje "
"indatageometri. Klusterindelningen delar in geometrierna i uppsättningar där"
" varje geometri ligger inom angivet <varname>distance</varname> från minst "
"en annan geometri i samma kluster. Avstånden är kartesiska avstånd i SRID-"
"enheterna."

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"ST_ClusterWithinWin is equivalent to running <xref "
"linkend=\"ST_ClusterDBSCAN\"/> with <code>minpoints =&gt; 0</code>."
msgstr ""
"ST_ClusterWithinWin motsvarar att köra <xref linkend=\"ST_ClusterDBSCAN\"/> "
"med <code>minpoints =&gt; 0</code>."

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Changed: 2.1.0 As a result of the introduction of geography support, the "
"usage <code>ST_Segmentize('LINESTRING(1 2, 3 4)', 0.5)</code> causes an "
"ambiguous function error. The input needs to be properly typed as a geometry"
" or geography. Use ST_GeomFromText, ST_GeogFromText or a cast to the "
"required type (e.g. <code>ST_Segmentize('LINESTRING(1 2, 3 4)'::geometry, "
"0.5) )</code>"
msgstr ""
"Ändrad i 2.1.0: Införandet av geografistöd gör att "
"<code>ST_Segmentize('LINESTRING(1 2, 3 4)', 0.5)</code> orsakar ett "
"tvetydigt funktionsfel. Indata måste typas korrekt som geometri eller "
"geografi. Använd ST_GeomFromText, ST_GeogFromText eller en typomvandling "
"till nödvändig typ, till exempel <code>ST_Segmentize('LINESTRING(1 2, 3 "
"4)'::geometry, 0.5) )</code>"

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Returned <varname>POLYGON</varname> geometries will always be clockwise "
"oriented."
msgstr ""
"Återlämnade <varname>POLYGON</varname>-geometrier är alltid orienterade "
"medurs."

#. Tag: para
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <varname>ST_PointFromWKB</varname> function, takes a well-known binary "
"representation of geometry and a Spatial Reference System ID "
"(<varname>SRID</varname>) and creates an instance of the appropriate "
"geometry type - in this case, a <varname>POINT</varname> geometry. This "
"function plays the role of the Geometry Factory in SQL."
msgstr ""
"Funktionen <varname>ST_PointFromWKB</varname> tar en välkänd binär "
"representation av geometri och ett Spatial Reference System ID "
"(<varname>SRID</varname>) och skapar en instans av lämplig geometrityp, i "
"detta fall en <varname>POINT</varname>-geometri. Funktionen har samma roll "
"som Geometry Factory i SQL."
